extends Node

# ============================================================
# ATTACK VFX — a Mystery Dungeon move effect for every attack
# ============================================================
# The frames live in Image_Assets/Attack_Effects/<Effect>[/<Part>]/NNN.png. Which effect an attack
# plays, and how, is DATA in Attack_Animation_Data/ -- generated by Scripts/Utilities/attack_vfx_build.py,
# which is where recipes and the attack -> recipe choices are edited (see the format notes at its top):
#   vfx_manifest.json    part -> frame file names + frame size
#   vfx_recipes.json     recipe -> body motion, reaction, element, screen effects, effect steps;
#                        status overlays; type fallbacks; element colours
#   attack_vfx_map.json  attack name -> recipe (+ per-type variants, its status conditions)
#
# WHEN IT PLAYS
#   - A damaging attack plays at the moment of the hit: play_attack_hit() hands over to play_hit().
#   - A non-damaging attack plays at the "X used Y!" beat, in place of the old Card_FX gesture.
#   - A Special Condition plays its overlay when it actually lands (Card_FX.status -> play_status).
# play_attack_intent() records the attack as PENDING for its attacker; the first hit by that attacker
# in the same turn consumes it, so a second hit (both Defending Pokémon, a bench hit...) is a plain lunge.
#
# HOW IT PLAYS
#   The cards move on Card_FX ghosts (Card_FX.motion): the attacker's BODY (contact bodies dart into the
#   defender and the target-side effects fire on the bump; the others move on the spot while the effects
#   play), then the defender's REACTION when the impact lands -- a flash and a lingering tint in the
#   attack's ELEMENT colour, and a knock-back / spin / lift / squash / jolt... Weakness and Resistance
#   double / halve the reaction and keep their green / red flash. SCREEN effects dim the board, flash it
#   or shake it. The effect frames are throw-away Sprite2Ds in one layer over the board (FX_Z: above the
#   card ghosts, below the message box and chrome). All times go through GameState.match_time().

